#################################################################
#  v5.9.0 — packages, sprint plans and kick-off, before any work.
#
#  Measured first: 9 stories, 27 points, and the last closed
#  iteration declared a capacity of 9. Twenty-seven does not fit
#  one box, so the work is split across three — G9, and the same
#  arithmetic that opened It6 last time.
#
#  Stories are taken in SCORE ORDER: EP21 at 8.00 before EP22 and
#  EP23 at 6.00, before EP24 at 4.00 and EP25 at 3.00. The order
#  falls out of the register rather than being chosen.
#
#  Two packages, grouped by capability rather than by time box:
#  what an adopter can RECEIVE separately.
#################################################################

fw:Pkg_GovernanceQueryable a backlog:Package ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "BRF-PKG-GOV" ;
    backlog:hasTitle "Governance and classification in the ontology" ;
    backlog:hasPackageVersion "1.110.0" ;
    backlog:memberOfContainer fw:Register ;
    backlog:targetsIteration fw:It7 , fw:It8 ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective fw:Obj_RulingsQueryable ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ;
    backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "A package is a grouping; its members carry the scores." ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Releasable on its own: an adopter gains the ability to QUERY the 18 rulings and the 23 classification tables rather than read them. The two ship together because a ruling that names no classification term is half an answer — asking which rulings govern task types requires both." .

fw:Pkg_ExecutionInOntology a backlog:Package ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "BRF-PKG-EXEC" ;
    backlog:hasTitle "Rule execution and description checking" ;
    backlog:hasPackageVersion "1.113.0" ;
    backlog:memberOfContainer fw:Register ;
    backlog:targetsIteration fw:It8 , fw:It9 ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective fw:Obj_RulesDecidedInCode ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ;
    backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "A package is a grouping; its members carry the scores." ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Separate release because it changes BEHAVIOUR rather than vocabulary: after it, a rule's outcome is decided by the ontology and a standard row that contradicts the TBox is reported. An adopter can take the first package and not this one — they gain queryable governance without their gate behaving differently, which is a real choice and the reason the two are not one package." .

